On Saturday I get up early.
I have to help in the café today.
But Bruno is here.
Before my shift he definitely needs a walk.
First, we go outside together.
We go for a short walk around the block.
I put him on the lead.
Sabine says he must always stay on the lead.
Back in the flat, Bruno is very hungry.
He whines quietly and wants his breakfast.
I open the dog food for him.
Bruno jumps up at me excitedly.
"Sit!", I say to him strictly.
He has to wait.
He looks at me and sits down immediately.
I put the bowl on the floor.
Now I can head to the café shortly.
